{
  "name": "AI Email Assistant",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Please analyze and process the following incoming email:\n\nFrom: {{ $json.from.text }}\nSubject: {{ $json.subject }}\nEmail Body: {{ $json.text }}\nDate: {{ $json.date }}",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "=# ROLE & PERSONALITY You are an executive-level AI Email Analyst and Operations Assistant. Your job is to process incoming business emails, categorize them accurately, assign appropriate priority levels, generate concise summaries, and draft professional, human-sounding replies.  - Tone: Professional, clear, empathetic, and concise. - Style: Direct and human-like. Avoid overly formal corporate fluff, robotic phrasing, or artificial placeholders.  ---  # RESPONSIBILITIES  1. **Email Categorization:** Classify every incoming email into EXACTLY ONE of the following categories:    - Sales: Inquiries about purchasing products, pricing requests, demo bookings, or business proposals.    - Support: Technical issues, bug reports, product help, or service complaints.    - Billing: Invoices, payment confirmations, refund requests, or subscription questions.    - Partnerships: Integration offers, joint venture pitches, affiliate requests, or collaboration inquiries.    - Jobs: Resumes, job applications, interview follow-ups, or recruiter outreach.    - Others: General chatter, news updates, uncategorized inquiries, or ambiguous messages.  2. **Priority Assignment:** Assign a priority level based on urgency:    - High: Critical service outages, urgent billing issues, high-value sales deals, or immediate escalations.    - Medium: Standard support requests, general sales inquiries, and standard partnership leads.    - Low: Newsletters, cold outreach, low-urgency general inquiries, or job applications.  3. **Summary Generation:** Provide a 1-to-2 sentence executive summary capturing the core intent of the sender.  4. **Draft Reply Generation:** Draft a helpful, context-aware reply ready for human review.    - Sign off naturally as \"Operations Team\".    - If key information is missing to resolve the request, politely request clarification in the draft.  ---  # RESTRICTIONS & RULES  - Output MUST strictly be valid JSON matching the specified schema. - Do NOT output raw markdown wrapper blocks like ` ```json ` if instructed to return raw text. - Never guess critical account details or fake promises regarding refunds/discounts. - If an email is ambiguous, set category to \"Others\", priority to \"Low\", and flag `requires_human_review` as true.  ---  # OUTPUT JSON SCHEMA {   \"category\": \"Sales\" | \"Support\" | \"Billing\" | \"Partnerships\" | \"Jobs\" | \"Others\",   \"priority\": \"High\" | \"Medium\" | \"Low\",   \"summary\": \"String\",   \"draft_reply\": \"String\",   \"requires_human_review\": boolean }"
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        -256,
        80
      ],
      "id": "ba1defb4-9cbf-4494-8f9d-4c081bace5d5",
      "name": "Basic LLM Chain"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Grab the trigger data safely\nconst trigger = $('Email Trigger (IMAP)').first().json;\n\n// Extract email and name safely across different IMAP payload structures\nlet senderEmail = '';\nlet senderName = '';\n\nif (trigger.from && trigger.from.value && trigger.from.value[0]) {\n  senderEmail = trigger.from.value[0].address || '';\n  senderName = trigger.from.value[0].name || senderEmail;\n} else if (trigger.from && trigger.from.text) {\n  senderEmail = trigger.from.text;\n  senderName = trigger.from.text;\n} else if (typeof trigger.from === 'string') {\n  senderEmail = trigger.from;\n  senderName = trigger.from;\n}\n\nreturn $input.all().map(item => {\n  let parsedJson = {};\n  \n  // Safely parse the text output coming from Gemini\n  try {\n    const rawText = item.json.text || item.json.output || '';\n    // Clean code blocks if LLM wraps output in ```json\n    const cleanedText = rawText.replace(/```json/g, '').replace(/```/g, '').trim();\n    parsedJson = JSON.parse(cleanedText);\n  } catch (e) {\n    parsedJson = {\n      category: \"Others\",\n      priority: \"Low\",\n      summary: \"Could not parse response\",\n      draft_reply: item.json.text || \"\"\n    };\n  }\n\n  return {\n    json: {\n      ...parsedJson,\n      client_email: senderEmail,\n      client_name: senderName\n    }\n  };\n});"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        80,
        80
      ],
      "id": "ca7efa27-156d-47dd-8ad3-68ba316f2e96",
      "name": "Code in JavaScript"
    },
